        "position": 4,
        "title": "Nothing special for extra price",
        "text": "Followed the sizing but it was waaaaay to big for our 80*lbs boxer. instead of supporting him evenly under his chest, belly, and hips, it was cutting into him around his legs creating pressure points. Plus it’s huge and heavy to carry around when hiking. It might be ok as some tactical gear for crazy stunts (the metal connectors, straps, stitching are heavy duty for sure. Seems like great quality to support heavy weights). But if you just hike a lot with your dog and need a compact plan B rescue harness for that one day when something might go wrong, this one is unnecessary. I’ll keep looking for more of a low profile and softer harness that can be more comfortable for an injured dog",
